:  \nLet's think step by step. 663 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.  \n1. Multiply 281 by the ones place digit **3** of 663:  \n   \\( 281 \\times 3 = 843 \\).  \n2. Multiply 281 by the tens place digit **60** (since 6 is in the tens place) of 663:  \n   \\( 281 \\times 60 = 16,\\!860 \\).  \n3. Multiply 281 by the hundreds place digit **600** (since 6 is in the hundreds place) of 663:  \n   \\( 281 \\times 600 = 168,\\!600 \\).  \n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 843 + 16,\\!860 + 168,\\!600 = 186,\\!303 \\).  \n\nSo, the final computed product is **186,303**.  \n\n**Note:** The initial guess of 186,304 is incorrect. The correct answer is **186,303** due to precise step-by-step addition.",
