+1=9 +1=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:5 +6=11 +1=12 \u2192 write 2, carryover1.\n\nTen-thousands: 2 (from 26,160's 2 in the ten thousands place?) Wait, 26,160 is 2 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 6 (tens),0. Wait, 26,160 is twenty-six thousand one hundred sixty, so the digits are:\n\n2 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nWait, but when adding to 5,886 (which is 5 thousands, 8 hundreds, 8 tens, 6 units):\n\nWait, maybe I should write them as:\n\n  0 5 8 8 6 (since it's only 5 thousands)\n\n+2 6 1 6 0 (26,160)\n\nSo adding each digit:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n6 +0 =6\n\nTens:8 +6=14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nHundreds:8 +1=9 +1=10 \u2192 0, carry1\n\nThousands:5 +6=11 +1=12 \u2192 2, carry1\n\nTen-thousands:0 +2 +1 (carry) =3.\n\nSo total is 32,046. Correct.\n\nAdding to 327,000:\n\n32,046 +327,000 = 359,046.\n\nHmm, but the user says they think it's 359,646. So maybe they have a different approach or made a mistake?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in the multiplication steps. Let me try another way: multiplying 654 \u00d7549 directly using the standard algorithm.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n      654\n\n    \u00d7549\n\n    ______\n\nFirst, multiply by 9 (units):\n\n654 \u00d79 =5,886. Correct.\n\nThen multiply by 40 (tens place, so shift one position left):\n\n654 \u00d74 =2,616 \u2192 \u00d710 \u2192 26,160. Correct.\n\nThen multiply by 500 (hundreds place, shift two positions left):\n\n654 \u00d75 =3,270 \u2192 \u00d7100 \u2192 327,000. Correct.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n5,886\n\n+26,160 \u2192 32,046\n\n+327,000 \u2192 total 359,046.\n\nHmm, so unless there's a miscalculation here, the correct answer should be 359,046. But the user's suggested answer is 359,646, which is 600 more. Maybe they added incorrectly?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up in the hundreds place multiplication?\n\nWait, let me try multiplying 654 \u00d7549 in another way, like breaking down both numbers.\n\n654 \u00d7