3).\n6 × 4 = 24 plus 3 is 27 (hundreds place). So that's 2,778. Adding two zeros gives 277,800.\n\nNow, I need to add all these results together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 1,389.\nSecond partial product: 41,670.\nThird partial product: 277,800.\n\nAdding them step by step:.\n\n1,389 + 41,670 = 43,059</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
