8 + 720,800 is 764,048, but maybe they subtracted instead? Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, perhaps in one of the multiplication steps.\n\nWait, maybe the original problem was 901*848?\n\nLet me do the multiplication another way to verify. Let's compute 901 * 848.\n\nAlternatively, use the standard algorithm:\n\nMultiply 901 by 848:\n\nFirst, write 901\n\nx 848\n\n------------\n\nStart with the ones digit: 8.\n\n901 *8 = 7,208.\n\nThen the tens digit: 4 (which is 40), so 901*40 = 36,040. Write shifted one position left.\n\nThen the hundreds digit: 8 (which is 800), so 901*800 = 720,800. Shifted two positions left.\n\nNow add them:\n\n7,208\n\n36,040\n\n720,800\n\nTotal:\n\n7,208 + 36,040 = 43,248\n\n43,248 + 720,800 = 764,048. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 764,048, but the user wrote 763,048. So perhaps they made a mistake in their calculation. Maybe when adding 43,248 + 720,800, they did 720,800 +43,000 = 763,800, then subtract  something? Not sure. Anyway, the correct answer is 764,048. So I need to point that out in the reasoning.\n</think>\n\n",
