al. The user might have made a mistake in their own calculation, so the assistant\'s job is to provide the correct solution following the template.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{153440}\n\n\nTo find the product of 274 and 560, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 274 by the ones place digit (0) of 560**:\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 274 by the tens place digit (60) of 560**:\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 60 = 274 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 1644 \\times 10 = 16440\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 274 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 560**:\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 500 = 274 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 1370 \\times 100 = 137000\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the step results**:\n\\[\n0 + 16440 + 137000 = 153440\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{153440}\\).', ''] 16%|#5        | 78/500 [1:57:28<10:03:09, 85.76s/it]
