lated somewhere. Alternatively, perhaps I made a mistake. Let me do 317 * 996 with standard multiplication:\n\n   317\n\nx 996\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 317 by 6: 1902\n\nThen multiply 317 by 90 (the 9 in the tens place): 28,530\n\nThen multiply 317 by 900 (the 9 in the hundreds place): 285,300\n\nAdding them: 1902 +28,530 = 30,432; 30,432 +285,300 = 315,732. So yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 315,732. The user might have thought 315,702, but that's incorrect. I'll proceed to write the reasoning steps accordingly, pointing out the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n",
