ssistant should present this step-by-step to show the correct method and result.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 855 and 483?\nI think the correct answer is: 712965  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 483 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.  \n1. Multiply 855 by the **ones place digit 3** of 483:  \n   \\( 855 \\times 3 = 2,\\!565 \\).  \n2. Multiply 855 by the **tens place digit 80** of 483:  \n   \\( 855 \\times 80 = 68,\\!400 \\).  \n3. Multiply 855 by the **hundreds place digit 400** of 483:  \n   \\( 855 \\times 400 = 342,\\!000 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 2,\\!565 + 68,\\!400 + 342,\\!000 = 412,\\!965 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **412,965**.",
