t 252,125. The user's thought answer is wrong by 10,000. Probably a miscalculation when adding the partial products. So I need to present the correct steps and show the accurate answer.\n\nAlright, so following the template provided, the reasoning should break down each step as multiplying by the ones, tens, and hundreds digits, then sum them up. The final answer is 242,125.\n</think>\n\n",
