 third partial product is 163,200.\n\nNow I need to add all three partial products together. Let me line them up properly:.\n\n   2176.\n+13600.\n+163200.\n----------.\n\nStarting with 2176 +13,600. Adding those: 2176 +13,600. Let's see, 13,600 + 2,000 is 15,600, then add 176 more to get 15,776. Then add that to 163,200. .\n\n15,776 +163,200. Hmm, 15k +163k is 178,700, then 776 +200 is 976. Wait, no, that might not be the right way. Let's do it step by step. 163,200 +15,776. Adding the thousands: 163,200 +15,000 = 178,200</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
