      "text": "441,463? Wait, wait a second. Wait 372,963 + 68,500 (since 368,500 - 300,000 =68,500). Wait no, sorry, I think I made a miscalculation here. Let me do it step by step.\n\nWait, 72,963 plus 368,500.\n\nFirst, 72,963 + 300,000 = 372,963.\n\nThen add the remaining 68,500 (because 368,500 is 300k +68,500).\n\nWait, actually, 368,500 is 300,000 + 68,500. Wait, but 368,500 is actually 300,000 + 60,000 + 8,500. Wait, perhaps better to do straight addition:\n\n368,500\n+ 72,963\n= ?\n\nAdding units:\n\n0 +3 =3\n\n0 +6 =6\n\n5 +2 =7\n\n8 +9 =17, so carry over 1.\n\n6 +7 +1 (carry) =14, so write 4 and carry 1.\n\n3 (from 368,500's hundred thousands?) Wait, let's see:\n\nWait, let's write them aligned:\n\n368500\n+ 72963\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 0 +3 =3\n\nTens: 0 +6 =6\n\nHundreds:5 +9 =14 \u2192 write 4, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:8 (from 368500's thousands) + 2 (from 72963's thousands) +1 carried = 11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:6 (from 368500's ten thousands) +7 (from 72963's ten thousands) +1 carried =14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place:3 (from 368500) +0 (since 72963 has no hundred thousands) +1 carried =4.\n\nSo total is 441,463? Wait, but the user thought the answer was 441,443. Hmm, so there must be an error in my calculation. Let me check each step again.\n\nWait, first, let's recheck the multiplication steps.\n\nFirst step: 737 x 9 (ones place):\n\n737 x 9: 700*9=6300, 30*9=270, 7*9=63. So 6300+270=6570+63=6633. That's correct.\n\nSecond step: 737 x 90 (tens place). 737x9=6633, then times 10 gives 66,330. Correct.\n\nThird step: 737 x 500 (hundreds place). 737x5=3685, so times 100 gives 368,500. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 6,633 + 66,330 = 72,963. Then adding 368,500 to that.\n\nWait, 72,963 + 368,500. Let me do this addition again carefully:\n\n368,500\n\n+\u00a0 72,963\n\n=?\n\nStart from the right:\n\nUnits: 0 +3 =3\n\nTens: 0 +6 =6\n\nHundreds:5 +9 =14 \u2192 4, carryover 1\n\nThou