n shift one position to the left (because it's the tens place), so 21,420. (Second partial product.)\n\nThird, multiply 238 by 600 (hundreds place, which is 6\u00d7100):\n\n238 \u00d7 6 = 1,428. Shift two positions to the left, so 142,800. (Third partial product.)\n\nNow, add all three partial products:\n\n714  \n21,420  \n+142,800  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \nTotal?\n\nAdding 714 + 21,420 = 22,134.\n\n22,134 + 142,800 = 164,934. \n\nSame result as before. So that must be correct. Therefore, the user's thought that it's 964,934 is incorrect. Probably a miscalculation when adding or maybe they multiplied 238 by 693 as (200+38)*(600+93), but that complicates more. Alternatively, maybe they added an extra digit somewhere?\n\nWait, 964,934 is over twice the correct answer. Let me see: 164,934 vs. 964,934. The difference is exactly 800,000. Hmm, that suggests maybe they did 238 * 4000 or something. Not sure. Anyway, according to my calculations, the correct answer is 164,934. So perhaps the user made an error in their thought process.\n\nTherefore, I'll proceed to write the step-by-step reasoning as per the template, showing each multiplication step and the sum leading to 164,934.\n</think>\n\n",
