s:  \n1. **Multiply 104 by the ones place digit (4):**  \n   \\(104 \\times 4 = 416\\)  \n2. **Multiply 104 by the tens place digit (90):**  \n   \\(104 \\times 90 = 104 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 936 \\times 10 = 9,360\\)  \n3. **Multiply 104 by the hundreds place digit (200):**  \n   \\(104 \\times 200 = (100 \\times 200) + (4 \\times 200) = 20,000 + 800 = 20,800\\)  \n\n**Sum all the step results:**  \n\\(416 + 9,360 + 20,800 = 30,576\\)  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(416 + 9,360 = 9,776\\); \\(9,776 + 20,800 = 30,576\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **30,576**.  \n\n**Note:** The initial guess of 34,576 is incorrect. The correct product is **30,576**.', ''] 40%|####      | 202/500 [4:49:06<5:58:11, 72.12s/it]
