0 + 360 is 3,960, plus 36 is 3,996. So yes, times 100 is 399,600. .\n\nNow I have the three parts: 444 (from the ones place), 35,520 (from the tens place), and 399,600 (from the hundreds place). I need to add them all together. Let me line them up properly:.\n\nFirst, the ones place result is 444. Since it's the ones place, it's just 444.\n\nThe tens place result is 35,520, which is shifted one position to the left (since it's the tens place), so that's correct as is.\n\nThe hundreds place result is 399,600, shifted two places left, so that's also correct.\n\nAdding them up:.\n\nStarting with the largest, 399,600.\n+35,520.\n= 435,120 (because 399,600 + 35,520: 399,600 + 30,000 = 429,600; then +5,520 = 435,120)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
