e's a discrepancy here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I made an error in the multiplication steps. Let me re-calculate each partial product.\n\nFirst partial product: 841 ×4.\n\n800×4=3200, 40×4=160, 1×4=4. 3200+160=3360+4=3364. Correct.\n\nSecond: 841 ×60.\n\n841 ×6 = 5046. Then ×10 gives 50,460. Correct.\n\nThird: 841 ×700.\n\n841 ×7. Let me re-calculate that: 800×7=5600, 40×7=280, 1×7=7. 5600+280=5880+7=5887. Then ×100 is 588,700. Correct.\n\nSo adding again: 3364 + 50,460 = 53,824. Then 53,824 + 588,700.\n\nWait, let's do 53,824 + 588,700:\n\n588,700 + 50,000 = 638,700\n\n638,700 + 3,824 = 642,524. Yes, that's correct. So the user's thought of 642,520 is off by 4. Hmm, maybe they made a mistake in adding. Let me see where.\n\nWait, perhaps I miscalculated the addition steps. Let me add the three numbers again:\n\nFirst: 3,364\n\nSecond: 50,460\n\nThird: 588,700\n\nAdding all three:\n\n3,364 + 50,460 = 53,824\n\n53,824 + 588,700:\n\n53,824 + 588,700 = ?\n\n588,700 + 50,000 = 638,700\n\n638,700 + 3,824 = 642,524. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the user's answer is wrong, and the correct answer is 642,524. Wait, but perhaps I made a mistake in one of the partial products.\n\nWait, let me try an alternative approach: multiplying 841 ×764 using another method.\n\nAlternatively, use the standard algorithm:\n\n\u2003\u2003\xa0841\n×\xa0764\n--------\nFirst, multiply by 4 (units):\n\n841 ×4 = 3364\n\nThen multiply by 6 (tens place, so ×60):\n\n841 ×6 = 5046 → shifted one position: 50,460\n\nThen multiply by 7 (hundreds place, so ×700):\n\n841 ×7 =5887 → shifted two positions: 588,700\n\nAdd them all: 3364 +50460 = 53,824; then +588,700 = 642,524.\n\nYes, so that's correct. Therefore the user's thought of 642,520 is incorrect, probably due to an addition error. The correct answer should be 642,524. But wait, let me check with a calculator to confirm.\n\nWait, since I can't use a calculator, maybe do another verification method.\n\nAlternatively, 841 × 76