of 786 (ones, tens, and hundreds places):\n\n1. **Multiply 949 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 6 = 5694\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   - \\(9 \\times 6 = 54\\) (write 4, carry over 5)\n   - \\(4 \\times 6 + 5 = 29\\) (write 9, carry over 2)\n   - \\(9 \\times 6 + 2 = 56\\) (write 56)\n\n2. **Multiply 949 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 80 = 75920\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   - \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\) (write 2, carry over 7)\n   - \\(4 \\times 8 + 7 = 39\\) (write 9, carry over 3)\n   - \\(9 \\times 8 + 3 = 75\\) (write 75)\n   - Add a zero to account for the tens place: \\(7592 \\times 10 = 75920\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 949 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 700 = 664300\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   - \\(9 \\times 7 = 63\\) (write 3, carry over 6)\n   - \\(4 \\times 7 + 6 = 34\\) (write 4, carry over 3)\n   - \\(9 \\times 7 + 3 = 66\\) (write 66)\n   - Add two zeros to account for the hundreds place: \\(6643 \\times 100 = 664300\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   5694 + 75920 + 664300 = 745914\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(5694 + 75920\\):\n     \\[\n     5694 + 75920 = 81614\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(664300\\):\n     \\[\n     81614 + 664300 = 745914\n     \\]\n\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{745914}\\).", ''] 49%|####9     | 247/500 [5:53:05<6:28:19, 92.09s/it]
