,864 is 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 4 (ones). So when adding:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 2 3 3 0 0\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 +\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 1 8 6 4\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 ------------\n\nAligning the digits:\n\nTen thousands place: 2\n\nThousands place: 3 +1 =4\n\nHundreds place:3 +8=11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:0 +6 =6 plus the carried 1 makes 7?\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out:\n\n23,300\n\n+\u00a0 1,864\n\n= (20,000 + 3,000 + 300 + 0 +0) + (1,000 + 800 +60 +4)\n\nAdding together:\n\n20,000 + (3,000 +1,000)=4,000 \u2192 total 24,000\n\nplus 300 +800 = 1,100 \u2192 total 25,100\n\nplus 60 \u2192 25,160\n\nplus 4 \u2192 25,164.\n\nAh! So the correct total is 25,164. Wait, so my previous calculation was wrong when I thought it was 25,284. So that's where I messed up earlier. So the correct answer should be 25,164. But the user thought it was 20,164. Hmm, so maybe the user made an error?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in breaking down the multiplication steps. Let me check the multiplication again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should try another method to confirm.\n\nAnother way: 233 \u00d7 108. Let's note that 108 is 100 + 8. So 233\u00d7100 + 233\u00d78 = 23,300 + 1,864 = 25,164. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer should be 25,164. Therefore, the user's thought of 20,164 is incorrect. Maybe they miscalculated 233\u00d78 as 1864, but then added wrong? Let's see, if someone thought 233 \u00d7 100 is 23,300, plus 233\u00d78=1,864, then 23,300 + 1,864: perhaps they did 23,300 + 1,800 =25,100, then added 64 to get 25,164. But if they instead added 23,000 + 1,800 =24,800 and then added 300+64=364, that would be 24,800+364=25,164. So yes, that's correct. So the user's answer of 20,164 is wrong. Probably they thought 233\u00d7100 is 20,300 instead of 23,300? Because 20,300 +1,864 would be 22,164. Not sure. Alternatively maybe they did 200\u00d7100=20,000, then 33\u00d78=264, 