y 90. So we need to multiply 764 by 90. Alternatively, multiply by 9 and then add a zero at the end. Let's do that.\n\n764 × 9:.\n- 9×4 = 36, write down 6, carryover 3.\n- 9×6 = 54 +3 =57, write down 7, carryover 5.\n- 9×7 =63 +5 =68. So that gives 6876. Wait, but since it's the tens place, this should be shifted one position to the left, so adding a zero makes it 68760? Wait, let's check again. .\n\nWait, actually, 764 × 90 is the same as (764 ×9) ×10. So 764×9 is 6876, then ×10 gives 68760. Let me confirm the multiplication:.\n\n764×9:.\n9×4 =36 (6, carry 3).\n9×6 =54 +3=57 (7, carry 5).\n9×7 =63 +5=68. So yes, 6876. So the second partial product is 68760.\n\nNow, moving to the hundreds place of 397, which is 3. Since it's the hundreds place, it's 300. So multiply 764 by 300. That's 764×3×100. .\n\n764×3:.\n3×4 =12 (2, carry 1).\n3×6 =18 +1=19 (9, carry 1).\n3×7 =21 +1=22. So that gives 2292. Then multiply by 100 gives 229200. So the third partial product is 229200.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products together:.\n\nFirst: 5348.\nSecond: 68760.\nThird: 229200.\n\nAdding them step by step. Let's add the first two first:.\n\n5348 + 68760. .\n\n5348 + 68,760. Let's see:.\n\n5348 + 68,760 = 68,760 + 5,000 = 73,760, then subtract the difference? Wait, no, perhaps better to do straight addition:.\n\n68,760.\n+  5,348.\n= ?.\n\nAdding the units:.\n0 +8 =8.\n6 +4 =10 (write 0, carry 1).\n7 +3 +1=11 (write 1, carry 1).\n8 +5 +1=14 (write 4, carry 1).\n6 +0 +1=7.\n\nWait, maybe I should line them up properly:.\n\n      68760.\n    +  5348.\n    ---------.\nStarting from the right:.\n0 +8 =8.\n6 +4=10 → 0 with carryover 1.\n7 (hundreds place) +3 (hundreds place from 5348? Wait, 5348 is four digits, so the thousands place is 5. Let me write it properly:.\n\n68760 is 6 8 7 6 0.\nplus 5348 is 0 5 3 4 8 (but shifted left by one because it's 5 thousands?).\n\nWait, actually, 5348 is 5 thousands, 3 hundreds, 4 tens, 8 ones. So when adding to 68760 (which is 6 ten thousands, 8 thousands, 7 hundreds, 6 tens, 0 ones):.\n\nSo:.\n\n       68760.\n     +  5348.\n     ---------.\n          8 (ones place: 0 +8).\n         6+4=10 → 0 with carryover 1.\n        7 +3 +1=11 →1, carryover 1.\n       8 +5 +1=14 →4, carryover1.\n      6 +0 +1=7.\nSo total is 74,108?.\n\nWait, let me do it step by step:.\n\nFirst number: 68760.\nSecond number: 5348.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:.\n\nOnes place: 0 +8 =8.\n\nTens place:6 +4 =10 → write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:7 +3 =10, plus the 1 carried over →11 → write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:8 (from 68760) +5 (from 5348) =13, plus 1 carried over →14 → write 4, carryover1.\n\nTen-thousands place:6 (from 68760) + 0 (since 5348 has no digit there) plus 1 carried over →7.\n\nSo the result is 74,108.\n\nNow add this to the third partial product, which is 229,200.\n\nSo 74,108 + 229,200.\n\nAdding these together:.\n\n74,108.\n+229,200.\n----------.\nAdding:.\n\nUnits: 8 +0 =8.\n\nTens: 0 +0 =0.\n\nHundreds:1 +2 =3.\n\nThousands:4 +9=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nTen-thousands:7 +2 +1 (carryover) =10 →0, carryover1.\n\nHundred-thousands:2 (from 229,200) + the carryover 1 →3.\n\nWait, let me write it properly:.\n\n229,200.\n+ 74,108.\n---------.\nStart from right:.\n\n0 +8=8.\n\n0 +0=0.\n\n2 +1=3 (hundreds place).\n\n9 (thousands place of 229200 is 9? Wait, 229,200 is 2 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 2 (hundreds?), wait no. Wait 229,200 is broken down as:.\n\n2 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait no:.\n\nWait 229,200 is 200,000 +29,200 → breakdown:.\n\nDigit places:.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nTens:0.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nWait, actually, 229,200 is:.\n\n2 (hundred thousands).\n\n2 (ten thousands).\n\n9 (thousands).\n\n2 (hundreds).\n\n0 (tens).\n\n0 (ones).\n\nYes. So adding to 74,108 which is:.\n\n7 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\