ucture it properly.\n\nFirst, note that 961 has three digits, so three steps. \n\n1. Multiply 618 by the ones place (1): 618 \u00d71 = 618.\n\n2. Multiply 618 by the tens place (60): 618\u00d760=37,080.\n\n3. Multiply 618 by the hundreds place (900): 618\u00d7900=556,200.\n\nThen sum all three results: 618 +37,080 +556,200 = 593,898. \n\nTherefore, the final answer is 593,898. The user's initial answer was off by 100, probably a miscalculation during addition. But following the steps correctly, that's the right result.\n</think>\n\n",
