ht. Alternatively, 218 × 500 = 218 × 5 × 100 = (200×5) + (18×5) ×100. Let me check:.\n\n200×5=1000, 18×5=90, so total 1090. Then 1090 ×100 is 109,000. Okay, so that's the third line. I'll write this shifted two places to the left.\n\nNow, adding up all three results:.\n\nFirst line: 218.\n\nSecond line: 13,080.\n\nThird line: 109,000.\n\nAdding them together. Let me do this step by step. .\n\nFirst, 218 + 13,080 = 13,298</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
