      "text": "280,588. Wait, but the user thought the answer was 980,588. Hmm, that's a discrepancy. Wait a second, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nWait, hold on. Let me redo the addition step. 273,300 plus 7,288. Let's break it down:\n\n273,300 + 7,000 = 280,300\n\nThen add the remaining 288: 280,300 + 288 = 280,588.\n\nHmm, so according to my calculation, the total is 280,588. But the user's answer is 980,588. That's way off. Did I make an error in the multiplication steps?\n\nWait, let me check the multiplication again. Let's recalculate each part carefully.\n\nFirst part: 911 \u00d7 8. Let's do it digit by digit:\n\n911 \u00d7 8:\n\nStarting from the right:\n1 \u00d7 8 = 8 (ones place)\n1 \u00d7 8 = 8 (tens place)\n9 \u00d7 8 = 72 (hundreds place). Wait, no, actually, that's not the right way. Wait, 911 is 9 hundreds, 1 ten, 1 one. So:\n\n1 (ones digit) \u00d7 8 = 8\n\n1 (tens digit) \u00d78 = 80\n\n9 (hundreds digit) \u00d78 = 7200\n\nAdding those: 8 + 80 = 88, plus 7200 is 7288. That's correct.\n\nSecond part: multiplying by the tens digit, which is 0. So 911 \u00d7 0 \u00d7 10 (since it's the tens place). So 911 \u00d7 0 = 0, then times 10 is still 0. So that's 0.\n\nThird part: hundreds digit, which is 3. So 911 \u00d73 \u00d7100 (since it's hundreds place). Let me compute 911 \u00d73 first.\n\n911 \u00d73:\n\n1\u00d73=3\n\n1\u00d73=3 (tens place)\n\n9\u00d73=27 (hundreds place)\n\nWait, actually, step by step:\n\n900 \u00d73 = 2700\n\n10 \u00d73 = 30\n\n1 \u00d73 = 3\n\nTotal: 2700 +30 +3 = 2733. So 911 \u00d73 =2733, then multiplied by 100 gives 273,300. That's correct.\n\nAdding them all: 273,300 + 0 +7,288 = 280,588. So that's the total. \n\nBut the user's answer is 980,588. Wait, that's three times as much. Hmm. Let me see where the mistake could be. Maybe I misapplied the place values?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the hundreds place. Let me think again. The hundreds digit is 3, so when multiplying, it's 300. So 911