0, and 40 × 700 is 28,000. Adding those together: 280,000 + 28,000 = 308,000. Wait, is that right? Let me check again. 440 × 700. Alternatively, 440 × 7 = 3,080, and then add two zeros because of the 700, so 3,080 × 100 = 308,000. Yep, that matches. Okay.\n\nNow, I need to add up all three results: 1760 (from ones) + 4400 (from tens) + 308,000 (from hundreds). Let's add them step by step. First, 1760 + 4400. 1760 + 4000 is 5760, then plus 400 more is 6160. Then add that to 308,000. So 308,000 + 6,160</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
