he standard algorithm to cross-verify.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       580\n    \u00d7 777\n    --------\nFirst multiply 580 by 7 (units place):\n\n580 \u00d77 = 4060. Write that down.\n\nThen multiply 580 by 70 (tens place). So shift one position to the left:\n\n580 \u00d77 =4060, so 4060 \u00d710 =40,600.\n\nThen multiply 580 by 700 (hundreds place). Shift two positions:\n\n580 \u00d7700 = 580\u00d77\u00d7100 = 4060\u00d7100 =406,000.\n\nAdding all together: 4060 +40,600 =44,660; then 44,660 +406,000 =450,660. So that's the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the user added wrong. Let me see what they thought the answer was: 450,460. Hmm, difference between my answer and theirs is 200. Where could that come from?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the multiplication steps? Let me try another approach. Let's compute 580 \u00d7777 as (500 +80) \u00d7 (700 +70 +7). Maybe expanding using distributive property.\n\nFirst, compute 500\u00d7700 = 350,000\n\n500\u00d770 = 35,000\n\n500\u00d77 = 3,500\n\nThen 80\u00d7700 =56,000\n\n80\u00d770 =5,600\n\n80\u00d77 =560\n\nNow sum all these:\n\n350,000 +35,000 =385,000\n\n385,000 +3,500 =388,500\n\n388,500 +56,000 =444,500\n\n444,500 +5,600 =450,100\n\n450,100 +560 =450,660.\n\nSame result. So the answer is definitely 450,660. The user's answer is 450,460, which is 200 less. Maybe they made a mistake in one of the multiplications?\n\nWait, let me see: perhaps in their calculation, they did 580\u00d7777 but messed up one of the steps. For example, if they thought 580\u00d770 is 40,600 (correct), but maybe they thought 580\u00d7700 is 404,000? That would give 404,000 +40,600 +4,060 = 448,660. Hmm, still not matching.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they miscalculated 580\u00d77 as 4040 instead of 4060? Let's see: 580\u00d77: 500\u00d77=3500, 80\u00d77=560, so 3500+560=4060. If they did 80\u00d77 as 560 but added wrong, like 3500 + 560 as 4060 is correct. So that's not it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 580\u00d770 as 40,600 (correct), but 580\u00d7700 as 404,000? Let's see: 580\u00d7700: 580\u00d77=4060, so \u00d7100 is 406,000. If they did 580\u00d77\u00d7100 but miscalculated 580\u00d77 as 4040, then 404,000. That would lead to total of 404,000 +40,600 +4060 = 448,660. Still not their answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they added wrong. Let me see their answer: 450,460. Let's see what 450,660 minus 200 is 450,460. So maybe they subtracted 200 somewhere.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps they thought the tens place was 7 instead of 70. Wait, the tens digit is 7, so 70. If they multiplied 580\u00d77 instead of 580\u00d770, that would be 4060, so adding that as part of the total. Wait, but then they would have three terms: 4060 (ones) + 4060 (tens) + 406,000 (hundreds). That would be 406,000 + 4060 +4060 = 414,120. Not matching.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they messed up the hundreds place. Wait, perhaps they thought 777 is 7 hundreds, 7 tens, 7 ones, but multiplied 580 \u00d7 700 correctly, but then maybe miscalculated the other terms.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did the multiplication as 580 \u00d7 700 = 406,000 (correct), then 580 \u00d7 70 = 40,600 (correct), but then 580 \u00d77 = 4060 (correct), but then added them as 406,000 + 40,600 = 446,600 plus 4060 would be 450,660. So that's correct. Hmm. Unless there's a different way they approached it?\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 580 \u00d7777 as (580 \u00d7 700) + (580 \u00d7 77). Let's see:\n\n580 \u00d7700 =406,000\n\n580 \u00d777. Let's compute that. 580\u00d770=40,600 and 580\u00d77=4,060, so total 40,600 +4,060=44,660. Then total product is 406,000 +44,660=450,660. Still same.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the user made an error in writing their own answer. Maybe they thought 580 \u00d7777 = (500\u00d7700) + (80\u00d7700) + (500\u00d777) + ... no, that's complicating.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps they thought 580 \u00d7 777 is 580\u00d7700 plus 580\u00d770 plus 580\u00d77, but miscalculated one of the terms. Let me see: if they miscalculated 580\u00