      "text": "131,596 + 800? Wait, no, wait. Wait, 70,800 is 70,000 + 800. Wait, no, 61,596 +70,800.\n\nAlternatively, let me do the addition step by step:\n\n61,596\n+70,800\n--------\nAdding ones: 6 +0=6.\n\nTens:9+0=9.\n\nHundreds:5+8=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:1 (from 61,596) +0 (from 70,800) + carried 1 =2. Wait, no, need to align properly.\n\nWait, let's write them aligned:\n\n61,596 is 6 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\n70,800 is 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nSo adding:\n\nTen-thousands place: 6 +7 =13.\n\nThousands place:1 +0=1.\n\nHundreds place:5 +8=13.\n\nTens place:9 +0=9.\n\nOnes place:6 +0=6.\n\nWait, that can't be right. Let me try again.\n\nWait, actually, 61,596 is:\n\nDigit places:\n\nDigit 1: 6 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit 2:1 (thousands)\n\nDigit3:5 (hundreds)\n\nDigit4:9 (tens)\n\nDigit5:6 (ones)\n\n70,800 is:\n\nDigit1:7 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit2:0 (thousands)\n\nDigit3:8 (hundreds)\n\nDigit4:0 (tens)\n\nDigit5:0 (ones)\n\nSo adding:\n\nTen thousands place:6+7=13.\n\nThousands place:1 +0=1.\n\nHundreds place:5+8=13.\n\nTens place:9+0=9.\n\nOnes place:6+0=6.\n\nSo putting together:\n\nStarting from the right: 6 (ones), 9 (tens), 13 (hundreds). Wait, but hundreds place is 5+8=13, so write 3 and carryover 1 to thousands.\n\nWait, maybe I need to do it step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes: 6+0=6.\n\nTens:9+0=9.\n\nHundreds:5 +8=13. So write down 3 and carryover 1.\n\nThousands:1 (from 61,596) +0 (from 70,800) +1 (carryover) =2.\n\nTen-thousands:6 (from 61,596) +7 (from 70,800) =13.\n\nWait, but 6 is in the ten thousands place? Wait, 61,596 is actually 6 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), etc. So the ten thousands digit is 6 and 70,800 has 7 in the ten thousands place. So when adding, ten thousands digits: 6 +7 =13. So the total is 13 in the ten thousands place? Wait, that would make the total as 132,396? Hmm, maybe I need to think