king down 187. Let me see:\n\nWait 187 is 1 hundred, 8 tens, 7 ones. So the hundreds digit is 1, tens is 8, ones is7. So that's correct. So the breakdown is correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the user made a mistake, but let me check the problem again. The user says:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 708 and 187?\nI think the correct answer is: 132399\n\nHmm. So there is a discrepancy here. Let me try another method to cross-verify.\n\nAlternative method: Let's compute 708 \u00d7187 using another approach, perhaps the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nWrite down 708 \u00d7187:\n\nStart by writing 708\n\n\u00d7187\n\n________\n\nFirst, multiply 708 by 7 (the ones digit):\n\n708 \u00d77 =4,956. (This matches earlier.)\n\nNext, multiply 708 by 8 (the tens digit). Since it's the tens place, this result is shifted one position to the left.\n\n708 \u00d78 =5,664. So written as 56,640 (since it's 80, so \u00d710).\n\nThird, multiply 708 by 1 (the hundreds digit), shifted two positions to the left (since it's 100):\n\n708 \u00d71 =708, so shifted two places gives 70,800.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n4,956\n\n56,640\n\n70,800\n\nTotal:\n\nAdd 4,956 +56,640 first:\n\n4,956 +56,640:\n\n4,956 +56,640. Let's see, 56,640 + 4,000 =60,640; then +956 \u219261,596. Then add 70,800:\n\n61,596 +70,800.\n\n61,596 +70,000 =131,596. +800 =132,396. So that's the same result.\n\nHmm, so either the user's thought answer is wrong, or I made a mistake. Let me try calculating with another method, maybe breaking down the numbers differently.\n\nAlternatively, compute 708 \u00d7187 as (700 +8) \u00d7 (100 +80 +7). But that might complicate, but let me try.\n\nAlternatively, compute 708 \u00d7187 as 708\u00d7(200 -13) =708\u00d7200 -708\u00d713.\n\n708\u00d7200 =141,600.\n\n708\u00d713 =708\u00d710 +708\u00d73 =7,080 +2,124 =9,204.\n\nSo 141,600 -9,204 =141,600 -9,000=132,600; then subtract 204 more: 132,600 -204=132,396. Same result.\n\nHmm, so that also gives 132,396.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps