nswer is wrong by 1.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I miscalculated? Let me check once again:\n\n263200 + 1974:\n\n263200\n\n+\xa0 1974\n\nStart from the right:\n\n0 +4 =4\n\n0 +7=7\n\n2 +9=11, write 1, carryover 1.\n\n3 +1 (carry) =4, plus 1 (from 1974\'s thousands place? Wait, let me write it vertically:\n\n263200\n\n+\xa0 1974\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n263200\n\n+\xa0 1974\n\n------------\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n0 +4 =4\n\n0 +7 =7\n\n2 +9 =11 → write 1, carryover 1\n\n3 (from 263200\'s thousands place) +1 (carryover) =4, but wait, let me see:\n\nWait, actually:\n\nThe numbers are:\n\n263200 has digits: 2 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nAdding 1974, which is 1 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nWait, so aligning:\n\n263200\n\n+\xa0\xa0 1974\n\nSo:\n\nOnes place: 0 +4 =4\n\nTens place:0 +7=7\n\nHundreds place:2 +9=11 → write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:3 +1 (from the 1974\'s thousands digit, which is 1) plus the carried over 1 → 3+1+1=5.\n\nTen-thousands place:6 remains as there\'s nothing to add except the carried over from thousands? Wait no, let\'s see:\n\nWait, maybe breaking it down digit by digit:\n\nPosition: hundred thousands | ten thousands | thousands | hundreds | tens | ones\n\n263200: 2 | 6 | 3 | 2 | 0 |0\n\n+\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 0 | 0 | 1 | 9 |7 |4 (since 1974 is 0 0 1 9 7 4)\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 0+4=4\n\nTens:0+7=7\n\nHundreds:2+9=11 → write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:3 +1 (from 1974\'s thousands place) +1 (carryover) =5.\n\nTen-thousands:6 +0=6\n\nHundred-thousands:2 remains.\n\nSo the total is 2 6 5 1 7 4 → 265,174. Yes, correct.\n\nTherefore the correct answer is 265,174, and the user\'s thought of 265,175 is incorrect by 1. So in the problem, since the user is asking to solve it correctly, I should provide the correct answer with the proper steps, pointing out where the user might have gone wrong if nece