0, plus 48 is 2808. Then adding two zeros gives 280,800.\n\nNow I need to add up all three parts: 3,744 (from the ones place) plus 14,040 (from the tens place) plus 280,800 (from the hundreds place). Let me add the first two first. 3,744 + 14,040. Let's see, 3,000 +14,000 is 17,000. Then 744 + 40 = 784. So total is 17,784. Then add that to 280,800. Hmm, 17,784 + 280,800. Adding 200,000 first gives 217,784, then add 80,800? Wait, no, maybe better step by step. 280,800 + 17,784. Let's break it down:.\n\n280,800 + 10,000 = 290,800.\n\n290,800 + 7,000 = 297,800</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
