\n\n4683 +33,450:\n\n4683 +33,450:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n  4,683\n\n+33,450\n\n=?\n\nAdding units: 3+0=3\n\nTens:8+5=13, write 3 carryover1\n\nHundreds:6+4=10 +1=11, write 1 carryover1\n\nThousands:4 +3=7 +1=8\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from 33,450\'s 3 in the ten-thousands place? Wait, 33,450 is 3 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 4 (hundreds),5 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nWait, 33,450 is 3 3 4 5 0.\n\nSo when adding 4,683 (which is 4 thousands, 6 hundreds, etc.) to 33,450 (33 thousands, 4 hundreds, etc.):\n\nBreakdown:\n\nThousands place: 4 (from first) + 33 (from second) =37 thousands.\n\nHundreds place: 6 +4 =10 hundreds.\n\nTens: 8 +5 =13 tens.\n\nOnes: 3 +0 =3.\n\nSo total: 37,000 + 1,000 (from 10 hundreds) =38,000. Then 13 tens is 130, plus 3 is 133. So total 38,000 + 133 =38,133. Correct.\n\nThen 38,133 +468,300.\n\nWait, 468,300 is 468 thousand, 300.\n\nAdding to 38,133:\n\n468,300 +38,133:\n\n468,300 +30,000 =498,300\n\n498,300 +8,133 = 506,433. So that\'s correct.\n\nHmm, so where did the user get 506,403? Let me check if I misread the numbers. The question is 669 and 757. Let me confirm the original problem.\n\nThe user wrote: "What is the product of 669 and 757? I think the correct answer is: 506403"\n\nWait, so perhaps I made an error in the multiplication steps. Let me try multiplying 669 and 757 another way, maybe the standard algorithm.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       669\n\n     x757\n\n     --------\n\nFirst multiply 669 by 7 (units place):\n\n669 x7 =4,683\n\nThen multiply 669 by 50 (tens place, so shift one position):\n\n669 x50 = 33,450 (as before)\n\nThen multiply 669 by 700 (hundreds place, shift two positions):\n\n669x700=468,300 (as before)\n\nNow add them:\n\n4,683\n\n33,450\n\n468,300\n\nAdding all together:\n\n4,683 +33,450 =38,133\n\n38,133 +468,300=506,433.\n\nHmm, same result. So maybe the user\'s answer is wrong, or perhaps I messed up.\n\nWait, let me try another approach: 669 *757. Maybe compute as (600+69)*(700+50+7). Let\'s expand t